            <ArticleTitle>Intrathecal capsaicin depletes substance P in the rat spinal cord and produces prolonged thermal analgesia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>481-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A single intrathecal injection of capsaicin depletes substance P from primary sensory neurons and causes a prolonged increase in the thermal and chemical pain thresholds of the rat but no apparent change in responses to noxious mechanical stimuli.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
